MCP server in MusE: handover
=============================

Status as of 2026-11-23, branch mcp-server (not merged into master). The server works and is tested;
what is missing compared to the GUI is listed in "Gaps" at the end, for deciding what comes next.


What it is
----------

A Model Context Protocol server inside MusE, so that an AI client (Claude Code, Claude Desktop, ...)
can read and change the song. Settings > MCP Server switches it on and shows the address, the token
and an activity log.

- HTTP on 127.0.0.1 only, one POST endpoint /mcp, JSON-RPC (no SSE, no sessions). A hand-written
  HTTP/1.1 layer on QTcpServer, JSON with QJsonDocument; the only new dependency is Qt5 Network.
- Off by default. Every request needs the bearer token. A foreign Host or Origin header is refused
  (DNS rebinding).
- Settings and token are in <config>/MusE/MusE/mcp.conf (mode 0600), not in the global config.
  A token shorter than 32 characters is replaced by a generated one when MusE starts.
- The tools are grouped in tiers that the user switches on in the dialog. A tool of a tier that is
  off is not even listed to the client.

Code:
  muse/components/mcpserver.{h,cpp}   HTTP, JSON-RPC, tiers, settings, McpTool
  muse/components/mcptools.cpp        all tools (registerMcpTools())
  muse/components/mcpdialog.{h,cpp}   settings dialog and activity log
  tests/mcp_smoke_test.py             test against a running MusE
  AGENTS.md                           short description for coding agents


The tools (63)
--------------

Read (always on):
  get_song_info, get_transport, list_tracks, get_track, list_parts, get_levels, measure_levels,
  list_audio_ports, list_markers, list_plugins, list_synths, list_plugin_presets, get_midi_notes,
  get_audio_part, get_tempo_map, get_drum_map, list_midi_ports, list_patches, get_export_status

Control (reversible, not undoable, applied like the mixer strips do):
  transport, set_position, set_loop, set_click, set_locators, set_track_mute, set_track_solo,
  set_track_volume, set_track_pan, set_plugin_param, set_plugin_on, set_patch, cancel_export

Record:
  set_track_record_arm, record

Edit (undoable unless the GUI's own action is not):
  add_track, rename_track, add_synth_track, move_tracks_to_folder, add_midi_part, move_part,
  add_midi_notes, modify_midi_notes, delete_midi_notes, add_plugin, save_plugin_preset,
  load_plugin_preset, add_route, remove_route (not undoable, like in the GUI), set_tempo,
  set_time_signature, set_tempo_map_enabled (not undoable), set_midi_track_output (not undoable),
  add_marker, modify_marker, delete_marker, undo, redo

Dangerous:
  delete_track, delete_part, remove_plugin, save_song, export_mixdown, export_stems

Exports write only inside the project folder of a saved song (links can not lead out), replace a
file only with overwrite: true, and run one at a time: the tool starts the export and answers at
once, get_export_status follows it, cancel_export stops it.


Rules for adding a tool
-----------------------

- Tools run in the GUI thread. Change the song the way the GUI does: through Undo (applyOperation /
  applyOperationGroup) for undoable edits, PendingOperationList + msgExecutePendingOperations for the
  rest. Never touch song containers directly. Look for the GUI action that does the same and use its
  code path, so the result is identical.
- Pick the tier by consequence: read = no change; control = reversible and harmless; record = makes
  files by recording; edit = changes the song (undoable where possible); dangerous = deletes, writes
  files, or takes over the transport. Mark "not undoable" in the description where the GUI is too.
- Helpers in mcptools.cpp: schema()/prop()/trackListProp(), controlTool(name, description, schema,
  tier), trackFromArgs(), positionProps()/tickFromPosition() (tick, seconds, or bar and beat, as in
  set_position), positionJson(), markerFromArgs(), pathInProject(), outputFromArgs().
- The handler must call done() exactly once. It may do so later (measure_levels does), but a long
  job should rather start and answer at once, with a status tool (as the exports do).
- Descriptions are for the AI client: say what the tool does, what the arguments mean, units,
  ranges, and what is not possible. Errors are plain sentences that say what to do instead.
- Add the tool to the tier set in tests/mcp_smoke_test.py and test it there; put back whatever the
  test changes (undo, or restore the value).


Testing
-------

  tests/mcp_smoke_test.py PORT TOKEN

against a running MusE with the server on. Tiers that are off are only checked for not being listed.
The Edit tier makes scratch tracks (mcptest<pid>-...), the Dangerous tier deletes them again and does
the export tests in a scratch folder in the project folder, which it removes. It never records and
never saves the song.

A run headless, that passes completely (195 checks on 2026-11-23): use the stems test project and
give MusE a home of its own (without that it may quit while loading the song):

  WORK=/some/scratch/folder
  STEMTEST_WORK=$WORK tests/stem_export/run.sh build/muse/muse4     # makes $WORK/project and $WORK/home
  CFG=$WORK/home/.config/MusE/MusE
  printf '[General]\nenabled=true\nport=18765\ntiers=31\ntoken=%s\n' \
         $(python3 -c 'import secrets;print(secrets.token_hex(32))') > $CFG/mcp.conf; chmod 600 $CFG/mcp.conf
  HOME=$WORK/home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=$WORK/home/.config XDG_CACHE_HOME=$WORK/home/.cache \
  XDG_DATA_HOME=$WORK/home/.local/share QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen \
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<the build's folders with .so files> \
    build/muse/muse4 -b dummy -p -N -I -2 $WORK/project/stemtest.med &
  tests/mcp_smoke_test.py 18765 $(sed -n 's/^token=//p' $CFG/mcp.conf)

With the default (empty) template instead, get_song_info and list_tracks fail for lack of tracks,
and with -a the transport did not run, so the transport, volume and pan checks failed; the code
before the marker work failed the same checks there.


Known limitations and open points
---------------------------------

- A range downmix is a little longer than the range: the bounce records whole audio cycles
  (176640 frames for 176400 with 256-frame cycles). The GUI downmix does the same. Stems are exact.
- Cancelling in the middle of a rendering stem/mixdown was not caught in a test (freewheel renders
  the test sections in milliseconds); cancelling before the first job was. It runs the same code as
  the progress dialog's Cancel button.
- MarkerMixdown and StemExport got begin()/report()/cancel()/finished() for the server. The GUI's
  stems path is covered by tests/stem_export/run.sh; the GUI's "one downmix per marker" path was not
  run after that change and is worth one manual try.
- Audio file import is not implemented (see Gaps).
- Marker ids (list_markers) are valid until MusE is closed.


Gaps: GUI functions without an MCP tool
---------------------------------------

From the menus of the main window, arranger, track list, mixer strips and the editors (piano roll,
drum editor, wave editor, list editor, master track, marker window). Fill in the priority column.
"Reuse" names existing code that a tool could call, so that it behaves like the GUI.

Missing:     not possible through MCP at all
Partly:      readable, or some of it possible

 #  Area / function                        State    Tier       Reuse                                   Priority
--  -------------------------------------  -------  ---------  --------------------------------------  --------
    AUTOMATION
 1  Read automation points of a parameter  Missing  read       CtrlList of AudioTrack::controller()
 2  Add / move / delete automation points  Missing  edit       UndoOp AddAudioCtrlVal, DeleteAudioCtrlVal,
                                                               ModifyAudioCtrlVal(List)
 3  Automation mode (off/read/write/touch) Missing  control    AudioTrack::setAutomationType()
 4  Clear automation, take snapshot        Missing  edit       MusE::clearAutomation(),
                                                               takeAutomationSnapshot()
    PARTS (arranger)
